This repository contains two kinds of material with different licences.

1. AI-SDLC template material (CC BY 4.0)

   The process files listed below are adapted from "The AI-SDLC Template and
   Method: AI-Assisted Software Development Life Cycle" by Andreas Martin and
   Sandro Schwander (FHNW University of Applied Sciences and Arts
   Northwestern Switzerland), https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22833065,
   licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence
   (CC BY 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

   Changes: adapted by Ayla Allen in 2026 (Python-only profile, lifecycle and
   PR advisory checks, CONTRIBUTING.md, rulesets, human review report, model
   tiers and related documentation); the git history records each change.
   These changes are also licensed under CC BY 4.0.

   Template material: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, LICENSE,
   skills/, scripts/, docs/INDEX.json, docs/STANDARDS.md,
   docs/AGENT-GUIDANCE.md, docs/future/, docs/specs/UC-TEMPLATE.md,
   docs/adr/ADR-TEMPLATE.md, docs/adr/ADR-000-python-as-project-language.md,
   .github/, .devcontainer/, .vscode/, environments/, .dockerignore,
   pytest.ini, tests/unit/test_architecture.py.

   Keep this section in projects created from the template: CC BY 4.0
   requires the attribution to stay.

2. Project material

   Everything else, in particular src/, tests/ (apart from the file listed
   above), docs/PROJECT.md, docs/TASKS.md, docs/specs/ and docs/adr/ files
   other than the templates, and README.md.

   Copyright (c) the project's authors.
